      "writtenOn": "2023-09-13T17:59:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I guess to answer your question another way--we are calling `SkChecksum::Hash32(\u0026key, sizeof(Key))` so every single byte of the key is incorporated into the hash so all of them need to be accounted-for. If the compiler decides to leave a padding byte as garbage it will affect the hash.\n\nIf we hashed each of the fields individually we would just ignore padding concerns, but in general Skia doesn\u0027t do this.",
      "parentUuid": "7838df2f_fe6e077d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 37,
        "startChar": 8,
